    luckyColor: "Navy Blue, Grey",
    luckyNumber: 5,
    luckyDay: "Wednesday",
    birthstone: "Sapphire",
    bestMatch: "Taurus, Capricorn",
    toughestMatch: "Sagittarius, Pisces",
    overview: "Analytical clarity and organization rule your day. You have sharp discernment, making this an optimal moment to streamline schedules, declutter, and fine-tune ongoing endeavors.",
    love: "Thoughtful acts of service and attentive care demonstrate your deep devotion more powerfully than grand words.",
    career: "Your precision highlights details others miss. Projects requiring audit, research, structure, or optimization progress smoothly.",
    health: "Prioritize digestive health with clean nutrition and mindfulness practice to quiet an overactive analytical mind.",
    cosmicAdvice: "Perfection is a process; celebrate every step of steady progress.",
    aboutTitle: "About Virgo — The Perfectionist of the Zodiac",
    aboutProse: ["Virgo is the sign of refinement — the one that notices what everyone else missed and quietly fixes it before anyone realizes there was a problem. Ruled by Mercury, planet of thought and precision, and grounded in Mutable Earth, Virgo combines sharp analytical thinking with genuine practicality. Where Gemini (also Mercury-ruled) scatters its mental energy across many interests, Virgo channels the same quickness into detail, order, and improvement.","Mutable Earth is an underrated combination: adaptable (Mutable) yet grounded (Earth). It produces people who can adjust to almost any circumstance while still staying practical and useful within it — the friend who reorganizes your kitchen during a visit, the coworker who catches the error nobody else saw."],
    personalityTraits: [{"strength":"Detail-oriented and analytical","shadow":"Prone to overthinking and worry"},{"strength":"Genuinely helpful, service-minded","shadow":"Can be overly critical, of self and others"},{"strength":"Practical problem-solver","shadow":"Struggles to relax or \"do nothing\""},{"strength":"Modest and hardworking","shadow":"Perfectionism can become paralyzing"},{"strength":"Reliable and organized","shadow":"Can come across as nitpicky"},{"strength":"Loyal once trust is earned","shadow":"Difficulty accepting help from others"}],
    personalityProse: "Virgo's mind is a genuine asset — few signs catch errors, patterns, or inefficiencies as quickly. The cost is that this same precision instinct rarely switches off, which means Virgo often applies the same exacting standard to itself that it applies to a spreadsheet, and self-criticism can run louder than it needs to.",
    loveProse: ["Virgo shows love through action, not declaration — running an errand, remembering a preference, quietly fixing a problem before it becomes one. This is a sign that can seem reserved early in a relationship, largely because Virgo wants to be genuinely sure before committing fully, not because the interest isn't there. Once trust is established, Virgo is devoted, dependable, and quietly generous in ways that often go unnoticed until you tally them up."],
    loveWants: "consistency, a partner who notices effort, honest communication over game-playing, and space to help without being told they're \"too much.\"",
    loveStruggles: "being told they're too critical, partners who are chaotic or unreliable, and voicing needs instead of just quietly fixing things themselves.",
    compatibilityChart: [{"sign":"Taurus","stars":"★★★★★","why":"Two Earth signs building something steady, sensible, and lasting together."},{"sign":"Capricorn","stars":"★★★★★","why":"Shared work ethic and practicality — a genuinely efficient, devoted match."},{"sign":"Cancer","stars":"★★★★☆","why":"Virgo's quiet care and Cancer's nurturing instincts complement each other well."},{"sign":"Scorpio","stars":"★★★★☆","why":"Both value depth and loyalty over surface-level connection."},{"sign":"Virgo","stars":"★★★☆☆","why":"Deeply understanding of each other, if both resist over-analyzing the relationship itself."},{"sign":"Pisces","stars":"★★★☆☆","why":"Opposite signs — Pisces' dreaminess can either complete or frustrate Virgo's practicality."},{"sign":"Leo","stars":"★★☆☆☆","why":"Virgo's critical eye can wound Leo's pride faster than intended."},{"sign":"Aries","stars":"★★☆☆☆","why":"Aries' impulsiveness clashes with Virgo's need for a plan."},{"sign":"Libra","stars":"★★☆☆☆","why":"Both Venus/Mercury-influenced, but indecision on both sides can stall things."},{"sign":"Sagittarius","stars":"★★☆☆☆","why":"Sagittarius' spontaneity unsettles Virgo's need for structure."},{"sign":"Gemini","stars":"★★☆☆☆","why":"Both Mercury-ruled, but Gemini's scattered energy frustrates detail-focused Virgo."},{"sign":"Aquarius","stars":"★★☆☆☆","why":"Aquarius' unpredictability doesn't sit well with Virgo's need for reliability."}],
    careerProse: ["Virgo excels in careers that reward precision and genuine usefulness: healthcare, editing, accounting, research, quality assurance, nutrition, administration, project management. This is a sign that often ends up as the person a team can't function without — not the loudest name on the org chart, but the one keeping everything actually running.","With money, Virgo is careful and methodical, usually one of the better budgeters in the zodiac, tracking expenses with the same precision applied to everything else. The risk isn't overspending so much as excessive worry about money even when the numbers are genuinely fine — Virgo's analytical mind doesn't always know when to stop checking."],
    healthProse: ["Ruled by the digestive system, Virgo is prone to stomach issues, IBS, and stress that manifests physically — this is a sign whose gut quite literally reflects its mental state. Because Virgo's mind rarely stops analyzing, structured relaxation (rather than vague \"just relax\" advice) actually works better — a set yoga class, a specific meditation routine, a defined wind-down ritual. Virgo also benefits from deliberately scheduling unproductive time, since left unstructured, the instinct to optimize and improve rarely takes a day off on its own."],
    genderComparison: [{"category":"In love","man":"Shows love through quiet acts of service","woman":"Cautious at first, deeply loyal once committed"},{"category":"At work","man":"Meticulous, the one who catches every error","woman":"Organized multitasker, quietly indispensable"},{"category":"Under stress","man":"Overanalyzes, withdraws to fix it alone","woman":"Becomes self-critical, needs reassurance"},{"category":"Best trait","man":"Reliable precision","woman":"Practical, grounded devotion"}],
    famousPeople: ["Beyoncé","Zendaya","Keanu Reeves","Freddie Mercury","Mother Teresa","Warren Buffett","Ariana Grande's frequent co-sign in fan discussions","Blake Lively"],
    faqs: [{"question":"What does it mean to be a Virgo?","answer":"Being a Virgo means being ruled by Mercury and Mutable Earth — a combination that produces detail-oriented, practical people who express care through action and precision."},{"question":"What is Virgo's zodiac element?","answer":"Earth, shared with Taurus and Capricorn — the three signs known for practicality, reliability, and building things that last."},{"question":"Who should a Virgo marry?","answer":"Fellow Earth signs Taurus and Capricorn tend to match Virgo's values and pace most naturally, while Water signs Cancer and Scorpio bring emotional depth Virgo quietly craves."},{"question":"What is Virgo's biggest weakness?","answer":"Perfectionism — Virgo's high standards can tip into excessive self-criticism or difficulty accepting anything, including their own effort, as \"good enough.\""},{"question":"Is Virgo a cold zodiac sign?","answer":"Virgo can come across as reserved, but it's rarely coldness — this is a sign that shows love through practical action rather than open declaration, which is easy to miss if you're expecting grand gestures."}]
