    toughestMatch: "Cancer, Capricorn",
    overview: "Venus promotes harmony, aesthetic beauty, and diplomacy across your social sphere. Your diplomatic grace helps resolve past misunderstandings effortlessly.",
    love: "Romantic harmony peaks today. Equal exchange, shared aesthetic pleasures, and mutual respect strengthen your key relationships.",
    career: "Collaboration and partnership bring outstanding success. Mediating agreements or designing refined presentations works in your favor.",
    health: "Balance active movement with peaceful relaxation. Yoga or a scenic stroll brings mental clarity.",
    cosmicAdvice: "Cultivate inner balance first; external harmony will naturally reflect it.",
    aboutTitle: "About Libra — The Diplomat of the Zodiac",
    aboutProse: ["Libra is the only sign represented by an object rather than a creature — the Scales — and it fits: this is the sign built around balance, fairness, and the art of seeing every side of a question before landing anywhere near an answer. Ruled by Venus and grounded in Cardinal Air, Libra initiates through relationship and harmony rather than force. Where Aries starts a fight, Libra starts a negotiation.","Cardinal Air is a genuinely social combination — the drive to begin (Cardinal) channeled through connection and ideas (Air). It produces natural mediators, people who instinctively read a room's emotional temperature and know exactly what needs saying to smooth it over, sometimes before they've even worked out what they themselves want."],
    personalityTraits: [{"strength":"Diplomatic and fair-minded","shadow":"Chronic indecisiveness"},{"strength":"Charming, socially graceful","shadow":"Can people-please at their own expense"},{"strength":"Genuinely values harmony and justice","shadow":"Avoids necessary conflict"},{"strength":"Aesthetically gifted, appreciates beauty","shadow":"Can prioritize image over substance"},{"strength":"Excellent at seeing multiple perspectives","shadow":"Struggles to know their own mind without input"},{"strength":"Warm, easy to talk to","shadow":"Prone to codependency in relationships"}],
    personalityProse: "Libra's gift for balance is real — this is a sign that can genuinely defuse a tense room. The tradeoff is that seeing every side of an argument makes picking one exhausting, and Libra can spend so much energy managing everyone else's comfort that its own needs get quietly deprioritized.",
    loveProse: ["Libra is the zodiac's natural romantic — ruled by Venus, genuinely happiest in partnership, and often happiest when there's someone to share decisions with. This isn't a sign that thrives alone by choice; Libra's identity is partly relational, built in dialogue with a partner, and the 7th House (Libra's own house) governs marriage and one-on-one relationships directly. Libra brings real charm, thoughtfulness, and fairness to love — but can also avoid conflict so thoroughly that resentment builds quietly underneath a calm surface."],
    loveWants: "harmony, a true partnership of equals, romance and aesthetic thoughtfulness, and a partner who initiates decisions occasionally so Libra isn't carrying that weight alone.",
    loveStruggles: "confrontation, decisiveness under pressure, and being honest about dissatisfaction instead of just keeping the peace.",
    compatibilityChart: [{"sign":"Gemini","stars":"★★★★★","why":"Two Air signs who talk easily and think alike — light, social, and stimulating."},{"sign":"Aquarius","stars":"★★★★★","why":"Shared love of ideas and fairness; an intellectually rich match."},{"sign":"Leo","stars":"★★★★☆","why":"Leo's warmth flatters Libra's romantic, aesthetic side."},{"sign":"Sagittarius","stars":"★★★★☆","why":"Both social and optimistic, with a shared love of new experiences."},{"sign":"Libra","stars":"★★★☆☆","why":"Charming and harmonious, though decision-making together can stall entirely."},{"sign":"Aries","stars":"★★★☆☆","why":"Opposite signs — magnetic pull, but Aries' speed can outpace Libra's need to weigh options."},{"sign":"Virgo","stars":"★★☆☆☆","why":"Both Venus/Mercury-influenced, but indecision on both sides can stall things."},{"sign":"Pisces","stars":"★★☆☆☆","why":"Both romantic, but Pisces' emotional depth can overwhelm Libra's need for lightness."},{"sign":"Capricorn","stars":"★★☆☆☆","why":"Capricorn's directness can feel harsh against Libra's diplomatic instincts."},{"sign":"Cancer","stars":"★★☆☆☆","why":"Cancer's need for direct reassurance and Libra's conflict-avoidance rarely align."},{"sign":"Taurus","stars":"★★☆☆☆","why":"Both Venus-ruled, but paces differ sharply — Taurus fixed, Libra changeable."},{"sign":"Scorpio","stars":"★★☆☆☆","why":"Scorpio's intensity and demand for depth can unsettle Libra's need for ease."}],
    careerProse: ["Libra thrives in careers built around fairness, aesthetics, and relationship management: law, diplomacy, design, PR, human resources, counseling, art curation, hospitality. This is a sign that often does its best work as a mediator or connector — the person who can get two opposing parties to actually agree on something.","With money, Libra has genuine taste and can be drawn to quality over quantity, sometimes overspending on beautiful things or social experiences in pursuit of a pleasant, balanced life. Financial decision-making can also be slow for Libra, since weighing every option is instinctive — setting simple rules or deadlines helps counter the tendency to deliberate indefinitely."],
    healthProse: ["Ruled by the kidneys and lower back, Libra benefits from proper hydration and posture-conscious movement — yoga and Pilates suit this sign particularly well. Because Libra's mental energy goes so heavily into managing relationships and decisions, mental fatigue is a more common complaint than physical exhaustion; genuine alone time, not typically Libra's first instinct, is often exactly what restores balance. Beauty and environment matter more to Libra's wellbeing than to most signs — a cluttered, ugly space genuinely affects this sign's mood."],
    genderComparison: [{"category":"In love","man":"Romantic and attentive, avoids conflict","woman":"Charming and fair-minded, seeks true partnership"},{"category":"At work","man":"Natural mediator, dislikes office conflict","woman":"Diplomatic, excels at building consensus"},{"category":"Under stress","man":"Becomes indecisive, avoids the issue","woman":"People-pleases past her own limit"},{"category":"Best trait","man":"Genuine fairness","woman":"Effortless social grace"}],
    famousPeople: ["Kim Kardashian","Will Smith","Bruno Mars","Gwen Stefani","Kate Winslet","Serena Williams","Mahatma Gandhi"],
    faqs: [{"question":"What does it mean to be a Libra?","answer":"Being a Libra means being ruled by Venus and Cardinal Air — a combination that produces charming, fair-minded people who initiate through relationship, diplomacy, and a genuine love of balance."},{"question":"What is Libra's zodiac element?","answer":"Air, shared with Gemini and Aquarius — the three signs known for intellect, communication, and social connection."},{"question":"Who should a Libra marry?","answer":"Fellow Air signs Gemini and Aquarius tend to match Libra's pace and values most naturally, while Fire signs Leo and Sagittarius bring warmth and energy Libra finds appealing."},{"question":"What is Libra's biggest weakness?","answer":"Indecisiveness — Libra's ability to see every side of a situation can make even small choices feel disproportionately difficult."},{"question":"Is Libra a two-faced zodiac sign?","answer":"Libra's instinct to keep the peace can look like inconsistency, but it's usually genuine conflict-avoidance rather than dishonesty — Libra will often agree in the moment and only voice real disagreement once it feels safe to do so."}]
