    careerProse: ["Scorpio excels in careers that reward investigation, transformation, and high stakes: psychology, research, surgery, detective work, finance, crisis management, forensics. This is a sign that doesn't shy from complexity or intensity — Scorpio often does its best work in situations other signs actively avoid.","With money, Scorpio tends to be strategic and private, rarely discussing finances openly but often quietly building resources and influence. Scorpio's comfort with risk (inherited from Mars and Pluto both) can pay off significantly, but the same intensity can turn into all-or-nothing financial decisions when Scorpio feels emotionally invested in an outcome."],
    healthProse: ["Ruled by the reproductive and eliminative systems, Scorpio's health often reflects how well emotional intensity is being processed rather than suppressed — this is a sign prone to holding onto stress physically when it won't (or can't) express it verbally. Intense physical outlets — strength training, martial arts, deep-tissue work — suit Scorpio's need to metabolize emotion through the body. Therapy or any practice built around genuine emotional excavation tends to resonate strongly with Scorpio, more than lighter, surface-level self-care."],
    genderComparison: [{"category":"In love","man":"Intense and possessive, tests loyalty before opening up","woman":"Magnetic and guarded, gives everything once trust is earned"},{"category":"At work","man":"Strategic, doesn't reveal his hand early","woman":"Perceptive, quietly influential"},{"category":"Under stress","man":"Becomes controlling or withdrawn","woman":"Becomes suspicious, needs proof of loyalty"},{"category":"Best trait","man":"Unshakeable loyalty","woman":"Emotional depth and resilience"}],
