    aboutTitle: "About Sagittarius — The Explorer of the Zodiac",
    aboutProse: ["Sagittarius is the sign of the horizon — always looking toward the next country, next belief system, next idea worth chasing. Ruled by Jupiter, the planet of expansion and luck, and built on Mutable Fire, Sagittarius combines restless enthusiasm with genuine adaptability. Where Aries burns fast in one direction, Sagittarius' fire spreads outward, curious about everything and reluctant to be pinned to just one path.","Mutable Fire is a rare, energizing combination: the willingness to change (Mutable) fueled by passion and optimism (Fire). It produces natural philosophers and wanderers — people who learn best by doing, who trust their gut over the rulebook, and who genuinely believe things will work out, often because for them, they usually do."],
    personalityTraits: [{"strength":"Optimistic and adventurous","shadow":"Can be tactless, speaks before thinking"},{"strength":"Honest, sometimes brutally so","shadow":"Struggles with commitment or routine"},{"strength":"Philosophical, big-picture thinker","shadow":"Prone to overpromising, underdelivering"},{"strength":"Independent and freedom-loving","shadow":"Restless, quick to lose interest"},{"strength":"Generous with knowledge and humor","shadow":"Avoids emotional depth by staying busy"},{"strength":"Genuinely open-minded","shadow":"Can be careless with others' feelings"}],
    personalityProse: "Sagittarius' honesty is a real strength — this is a sign incapable of the polite fiction most people rely on to smooth over conversations. The tradeoff is tact: Sagittarius often says exactly what it thinks the moment it thinks it, without pausing to consider how the truth will land, and freedom-seeking can look like commitment-avoidance to partners who need more certainty.",
    loveProse: ["Sagittarius falls for adventure as much as for a person — a partner who's up for a spontaneous trip, an unplanned conversation that runs until 3am, someone who doesn't need every detail mapped out in advance. This is a sign that resists anything that feels like a cage, and long courtships built on grand romantic promises tend to appeal less than genuine shared experience. Sagittarius loves honestly and openly, but needs real independence within a relationship to avoid feeling trapped."],
    loveWants: "freedom within commitment, humor, shared adventure, and a partner who doesn't take blunt honesty personally.",
    loveStruggles: "routine, being tied down too early, and reading the emotional weight of its own words before they land.",
    compatibilityChart: [{"sign":"Aries","stars":"★★★★★","why":"Shared love of freedom and adventure; neither tries to slow the other down."},{"sign":"Leo","stars":"★★★★★","why":"Both Fire signs matching enthusiasm for enthusiasm; big, warm, generous chemistry."},{"sign":"Libra","stars":"★★★★☆","why":"Both social and optimistic, with a shared love of new experiences."},{"sign":"Aquarius","stars":"★★★★☆","why":"Two independent spirits who genuinely respect each other's need for space."},{"sign":"Sagittarius","stars":"★★★☆☆","why":"Adventurous and free-spirited together, if both learn to sometimes actually stay put."},{"sign":"Gemini","stars":"★★★☆☆","why":"Opposite signs — great intellectual chemistry, but both resist commitment."},{"sign":"Virgo","stars":"★★☆☆☆","why":"Sagittarius' spontaneity unsettles Virgo's need for structure."},{"sign":"Pisces","stars":"★★☆☆☆","why":"Both dreamers in their own way, but rarely dreaming in the same direction."},{"sign":"Cancer","stars":"★★☆☆☆","why":"Sagittarius' need for freedom unsettles Cancer's need for closeness."},{"sign":"Capricorn","stars":"★★☆☆☆","why":"Capricorn's caution and Sagittarius' spontaneity rarely find a natural rhythm."},{"sign":"Taurus","stars":"★★☆☆☆","why":"Taurus craves roots; Sagittarius craves freedom — a genuine mismatch of needs."},{"sign":"Scorpio","stars":"★★☆☆☆","why":"Sagittarius' bluntness and need for freedom unsettle Scorpio's need for depth and loyalty."}],
    careerProse: ["Sagittarius thrives in careers that allow travel, teaching, or big-picture thinking: education, publishing, travel and tourism, entrepreneurship, sports, philosophy, international business. This is a sign that gets bored fast in rigid, repetitive roles and does its best work when given real autonomy to explore a subject or a market on its own terms.","With money, Sagittarius tends toward the optimistic and occasionally reckless — Jupiter's expansive influence can mean big wins but also careless spending on experiences (travel especially) over long-term saving. Sagittarius' natural luck is real, but building any actual financial cushion usually requires a level of structure this sign has to deliberately impose on itself."],
    healthProse: ["Ruled by the hips and thighs, Sagittarius benefits from activities that let the body move freely and cover ground — hiking, running, cycling, and any sport that gets this sign outdoors and away from routine. Restlessness is Sagittarius' most common wellness challenge: sitting still for extended periods (long work sessions, rigid schedules) drains this sign faster than physical exertion ever does. Travel itself functions as genuine mental health maintenance for Sagittarius, not just leisure."],
    genderComparison: [{"category":"In love","man":"Adventurous, needs independence within commitment","woman":"Honest and free-spirited, resists being tied down too soon"},{"category":"At work","man":"Big-picture thinker, dislikes micromanagement","woman":"Bold risk-taker, thrives with real autonomy"},{"category":"Under stress","man":"Runs from the problem, literally or figuratively","woman":"Gets blunt, needs space to process"},{"category":"Best trait","man":"Infectious optimism","woman":"Fearless independence"}],
    famousPeople: ["Taylor Swift","Brad Pitt","Nicki Minaj","Miley Cyrus","Jay-Z","Britney Spears","Winston Churchill"],
    faqs: [{"question":"What does it mean to be a Sagittarius?","answer":"Being a Sagittarius means being ruled by Jupiter and Mutable Fire — a combination that produces optimistic, freedom-loving people who learn through adventure and speak with unfiltered honesty."},{"question":"What is Sagittarius' zodiac element?","answer":"Fire, shared with Aries and Leo — the three signs known for passion, confidence, and enthusiasm."},{"question":"Who should a Sagittarius marry?","answer":"Fellow Fire signs Aries and Leo match Sagittarius' energy and optimism most naturally, while Air signs Libra and Aquarius bring the mental stimulation and independence Sagittarius values."},{"question":"What is Sagittarius' biggest weakness?","answer":"Tactlessness — Sagittarius' commitment to honesty can come out blunt or careless, especially when the sign hasn't paused to consider how the truth will land."},{"question":"Is Sagittarius afraid of commitment?","answer":"Not exactly — Sagittarius commits fully once genuinely convinced, but needs real independence within the relationship; what looks like commitment-phobia is usually a fear of feeling trapped, not a fear of love itself."}]
