    careerProse: ["Capricorn is arguably the zodiac's most career-oriented sign — this is a sign built for leadership, long-term strategy, and steady climb, thriving in law, finance, engineering, government, corporate management, and any field with a clear ladder to climb. Capricorn rarely expects success overnight and rarely gets discouraged by slow progress, which is exactly why it tends to outlast more impulsive competitors.","With money, Capricorn is naturally frugal and strategic, often the best long-term saver and investor of any sign, with genuine discomfort around unnecessary risk or impulsive spending. The tradeoff is that Capricorn can hold onto money out of anxiety even when financially secure, and needs to consciously practice enjoying the security it's worked so hard to build."],
    healthProse: ["Ruled by the bones, joints, and knees, Capricorn should pay particular attention to skeletal health and posture, especially given this sign's tendency to push through physical discomfort the same way it pushes through everything else. Capricorn's biggest health risk is often not injury but burnout — this is a sign that treats rest as something to be earned, and can run on empty far longer than is genuinely sustainable. Structured, goal-oriented fitness (strength training with visible progress, a formal program) tends to appeal to Capricorn far more than unstructured movement."],
    genderComparison: [{"category":"In love","man":"Reserved at first, deeply committed once serious","woman":"Guards her heart, tests reliability before opening up"},{"category":"At work","man":"Natural executive, plays the long game","woman":"Quietly ambitious, rarely seeks the spotlight for credit"},{"category":"Under stress","man":"Withdraws into work","woman":"Becomes overly self-critical or controlling"},{"category":"Best trait","man":"Unshakeable discipline","woman":"Grounded, realistic resilience"}],
    famousPeople: ["Michelle Obama","Kate Middleton","Denzel Washington","Dolly Parton","Timothée Chalamet","Muhammad Ali","LeBron James"],
