    cosmicAdvice: "Embrace your unique vision; original thinking changes the world.",
    aboutTitle: "About Aquarius — The Visionary of the Zodiac",
    aboutProse: ["Aquarius is the sign most often misunderstood, largely because it doesn't run on the emotional logic most of the zodiac does. Ruled by both Saturn (structure) and Uranus (disruption), and grounded in Fixed Air, Aquarius is a genuine paradox: unshakeably committed to its own convictions (Fixed) while constantly reimagining how things could be different (Air, Uranus). Despite the Water Bearer symbol, Aquarius is an Air sign through and through — this is about ideas, not emotion.","Fixed Air produces a rare kind of independence: people who think for themselves as a matter of principle, who resist groupthink even when it would be easier to go along, and who often care more about humanity in the abstract than about any single relationship in the specific — a trait that can look detached but usually comes from genuinely thinking on a bigger scale."],
    personalityTraits: [{"strength":"Original, thinks outside convention","shadow":"Can be emotionally detached or aloof"},{"strength":"Genuinely humanitarian, big-picture minded","shadow":"Struggles with close, one-on-one intimacy"},{"strength":"Independent, resistant to peer pressure","shadow":"Stubborn once a belief is set"},{"strength":"Intellectually curious","shadow":"Can seem unpredictable or contrary"},{"strength":"Loyal to causes and communities","shadow":"Avoids vulnerability by intellectualizing feeling"},{"strength":"Progressive, comfortable with change","shadow":"Can prioritize principle over people close to them"}],
    personalityProse: "Aquarius' independence of mind is a genuine strength — this is the sign least likely to follow a trend simply because everyone else is. The tradeoff is intimacy: Aquarius often processes emotion intellectually rather than viscerally, which can leave partners feeling like they're being analyzed rather than truly felt, even when the care underneath is completely real.",
    loveProse: ["Aquarius falls for the mind before the heart — a partner's ideas, values, and originality matter more early on than conventional romantic chemistry. This is a sign that resists the traditional relationship script, often preferring a partnership built on friendship and shared vision over grand declarations. Aquarius needs real independence within love; a relationship that feels like it's swallowing their individuality will drive this sign away fast, no matter how strong the underlying connection."],
    loveWants: "intellectual connection, a partner who respects independence, shared values or causes, and room to be unconventional without judgment.",
    loveStruggles: "emotional vulnerability, traditional romantic expectations, and expressing feeling in ways a partner can actually recognize as such.",
