    careerProse: ["Aquarius thrives in careers built around innovation, ideas, and social impact: technology, science, activism, engineering, nonprofit work, research, any field genuinely oriented toward the future. This is a sign that gets restless in rigid, hierarchical environments and does its best work when given the freedom to think differently and challenge the status quo.","With money, Aquarius is often unpredictable — capable of frugality on ordinary purchases but willing to spend generously on causes, technology, or community projects it believes in. Traditional financial planning can feel uninteresting to this sign, so tying savings goals to a bigger vision or cause tends to work better than generic budgeting advice."],
    healthProse: ["Ruled by the ankles and circulatory system, Aquarius should pay attention to circulation and lower-leg injuries, particularly given this sign's tendency to live largely \"in the head\" and neglect the body's basic signals. Aquarius' wellness is closely tied to intellectual stimulation and social connection to a community or cause — isolation affects this sign's mental health more than most, despite its independent streak. Novel, unconventional forms of exercise (something genuinely new or offbeat) hold Aquarius' interest far longer than repetitive routine."],
    genderComparison: [{"category":"In love","man":"Friend-first, needs independence within the relationship","woman":"Unconventional, resists being defined by a partner"},{"category":"At work","man":"Visionary, dislikes rigid hierarchy","woman":"Innovative, comfortable challenging the norm"},{"category":"Under stress","man":"Withdraws into his own head","woman":"Becomes detached, intellectualizes the problem"},{"category":"Best trait","man":"Original, forward-thinking mind","woman":"Fierce independence of thought"}],
    famousPeople: ["Harry Styles","Oprah Winfrey","Jennifer Aniston","Abraham Lincoln","Ed Sheeran","Alicia Keys","Charles Darwin"],
    faqs: [{"question":"What does it mean to be an Aquarius?","answer":"Being an Aquarius means being ruled by Saturn and Uranus with Fixed Air energy — a combination that produces original, independent thinkers who value ideas and humanity over convention."},{"question":"What is Aquarius' zodiac element?","answer":"Air, shared with Gemini and Libra — the three signs known for intellect, communication, and social connection, despite the Water Bearer symbol."},{"question":"Who should an Aquarius marry?","answer":"Fellow Air signs Gemini and Libra tend to match Aquarius' intellectual pace most naturally, while Fire signs Aries and Sagittarius bring the independence and energy Aquarius appreciates."},{"question":"What is Aquarius' biggest weakness?","answer":"Emotional detachment — Aquarius often processes feeling intellectually rather than viscerally, which can make genuine vulnerability harder to access and express than for more emotionally driven signs."},{"question":"Is Aquarius a cold zodiac sign?","answer":"Aquarius can come across as detached, but it's rarely coldness — this is a sign that cares deeply about people in the abstract and can struggle to translate that care into the smaller, more personal gestures a close relationship often needs."}]
